\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 1. Zero-RAM Partition Filtering\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 Instead of reading all 83.4 million rows into memory, PyArrow uses predicate pushdown filters to scan only the byte blocks belonging to the specific year being processed (2022 for train, 2023 for validation, 2024 for testing).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 2. Spatial Canvas Reconstitution\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 For every single day in the split, the script reconstructs California\'92s physical map. It creates a blank 2D canvas of shape 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 (403 rows, 352 cols)
\f1\fs24 \strokec2 \'97matching the discrete bounding box of the state\'92s 5km cells. It then maps the 9 environmental features into this matrix:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 4 weather layers (
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 t2m
\f1\fs24 \strokec2 , 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 rh2m
\f1\fs24 \strokec2 , 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 wind_speed_10m
\f1\fs24 \strokec2 , 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 tp
\f1\fs24 \strokec2 )\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 2 vegetation layers (
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 ndvi
\f1\fs24 \strokec2 , 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 evi
\f1\fs24 \strokec2 )\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 3 topography layers (
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 elevation
\f1\fs24 \strokec2 , 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 slope
\f1\fs24 \strokec2 , 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 aspect
\f1\fs24 \strokec2 )\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 \strokec2 3. Border Zero-Padding\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0 \cf0 When evaluating cells along the Pacific coastline or the state boundary, slicing a window around the cell would normally reach out of bounds. The script adds a boundary padding of radius r=3$(mode="constant", constant_values=0), ensuring every cell has a complete neighborhood.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 4. Prior-Day Lagged Patch Extraction ($t-1 \\rightarrow t$)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0 \cf0 To enforce zero temporal leakage, the script looks at the full (9, H, W) surface from 
\f3\b \strokec2 yesterday ($t-1$)
\f4\b0 \strokec2  to predict whether a fire ignited at the center cell 
\f3\b \strokec2 today ($t$)
\f4\b0 \strokec2 .\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Around the target cell's (x, y) coordinate, it cuts out a (2r+1) \\times (2r+1) = 7 X 7 grid window.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Because each grid cell is 5km, that 7 X 7 patch represents a physical 
\f3\b \strokec2 35 km X 35 km regional box
\f4\b0 \strokec2  centered directly on the target location.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 5. Output Array Generation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0 \cf0 The resulting patches and labels are saved as .npy arrays:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\'95	}- \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 X_train.npy:
\f4\b0  A 4D tensor with shape (N_samples, 9, 7, 7).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\'95	}- \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 y_train.npy:
\f4\b0  A 1D target vector with shape (N_samples,) where each value is 1 (fire ignited) or 0 (no fire).\
